Directory & File Conventions
All test code lives under e2e/.

Page Object Model (POM):

One page object per screen or feature flow: pages/<feature>.page.js

One spec file per scenario group: e2e/<feature>.spec.js

File Naming: Lowercase kebab-case filenames (e.g., login.page.js, cart.page.js, checkout.spec.js).

Module System: Use CommonJS (require / module.exports). Do NOT use ES modules (import / export).

Page Object export format: module.exports = { FeaturePage }; or module.exports = FeaturePage;

Spec file import format: const FeaturePage = require('./<feature>.page');

Code Style & Authoring Standards
Formatting: 2-space indentation throughout.

Page Object Structure:

Store locators as class properties inside the constructor(page) (e.g., this.usernameInput = page.locator('#username');).

Prioritize user-facing locators (getByRole, getByText, getByLabel) where appropriate, maintaining consistency with existing files.

Spec File Structure:

Wrap related test cases in test.describe('Feature Name', () => { ... }).

Use test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => { ... }) for navigating to [https://bstackdemo.com](https://bstackdemo.com) and performing shared setup/login.

Timeouts & Wait Strategies:

Use explicit timeout arguments on assertions when dealing with dynamic elements (e.g., await expect(element).toBeVisible({ timeout: 5000 });).

Avoid hardcoded sleeps (page.waitForTimeout()). Rely on Playwright auto-waiting and web-first assertions (expect).

Security:

Never hardcode real production credentials in committed code. Use placeholders or environment variables (process.env.BSTACK_USERNAME) where applicable.

If test fail send the report which test has faild and which line  .

